        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>made all shorthand properties have the same intro text:</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-md notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"The **`property_name`** CSS shorthand property ...&quot; \"><pre class=\"notranslate\">The <span class=\"pl-s\">**</span><span class=\"pl-s\">`</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">property_name</span><span class=\"pl-s\">`</span><span class=\"pl-s\">**</span> CSS shorthand property ...\" </pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">with CSS and shorthand being links.</p>\n<ol start=\"2\" dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Made all the constituent properties the same, starting with</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-md notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"This property is a shorthand for the following &lt;logical/physical&gt; properties:\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">This property is a shorthand for the following &lt;logical/physical&gt; properties:</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">generally they all start with</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-md notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"This property is a shorthand for the following CSS properties:\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">This property is a shorthand for the following CSS properties:</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">so this gets them closer to that.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45351",
            "title": "standardize \"CSS shorthand property\"",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T13:07:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T11:54:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replaces <code class=\"notranslate\">anticlockwise</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">counterclockwise</code> in the Canvas tutorial — five occurrences across two files, in the prose describing how to draw a shape with a hole in it and in two of the accompanying code comments.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The writing style guide requires American English spelling, and <code class=\"notranslate\">counterclockwise</code> is already the settled form here by 47 occurrences to 7. It is also the name of the parameter these very sentences are describing — <code class=\"notranslate\">arc()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">ellipse()</code> both take a boolean called <code class=\"notranslate\">counterclockwise</code> — so the prose now matches the API it documents.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The two remaining occurrences are deliberately untouched: the <code class=\"notranslate\">arc()</code> tutorial and the <code class=\"notranslate\">ellipse()</code> reference both write \"counterclockwise (anticlockwise)\", giving the British term alongside the parameter name for readers who know it by that word.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45350",
            "title": "Use American English spelling for anticlockwise",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T10:25:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T10:23:47.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "husamemadH",
                "url": "https://github.com/husamemadH"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87750369?u=ccc1f52005708ae16bcb50e325e02145bff0ef7d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Follow up on</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/mdn/discussions/911\">https://github.com/orgs/mdn/discussions/911</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5203572534\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45259\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45259/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45259\">#45259</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The PR updates writing guidelines to instruct contributors to not use the <code class=\"notranslate\">{{Deprecated_Header}}</code> macro anymore. Because, now the deprecated status banner is being inferred from front-matter <code class=\"notranslate\">status</code> property or data from web-features repository.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Contributors need to know.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/orgs/mdn/discussions/911\">https://github.com/orgs/mdn/discussions/911</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5203572534\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45259\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/45259/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45259\">#45259</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45345",
            "title": "chore: Update writing guidlines and remove Deprecated_Header macro mentions",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T08:45:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T08:29:10.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "OnkarRuikar",
                "url": "https://github.com/OnkarRuikar"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61856979?u=2ae56839a2779c62b750f6f2e1e049edb283def2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Replaces the format-by-format list on the img element page with concise guidance about choosing formats based on compression, browser support, and image requirements. It also explains fallbacks and the progressive-rendering benefit of JPEG XL for large images.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The previous list called several competing formats a good choice without clearly explaining how to decide between them. This revision directs readers to WebP or AVIF for raster compression, SVG for scalable graphics, and picture-based fallbacks where browser support requires them.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Markdownlint: passed</li>\n<li>Prettier check: passed</li>\n<li>Updated the affected internal heading link</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45286.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5221179468\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45286\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45286/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45286\">#45286</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45339",
            "title": "Clarify image format selection guidance",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T06:26:07.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T06:25:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "33modeling",
                "url": "https://github.com/33modeling"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61856979?u=2ae56839a2779c62b750f6f2e1e049edb283def2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds links to the input element and HTMLInputElement interface in the See also sections for the selectionStart and selectionEnd property pages.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This makes the property pages consistent with their HTMLTextAreaElement counterparts and gives readers direct links back to the related element and interface.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Markdownlint: passed</li>\n<li>Prettier check: passed</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45314.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5247285646\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45314\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45314/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45314\">#45314</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45338",
            "title": "Add input links to selection property pages",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-27T06:23:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-27T06:22:39.000Z",
